[PIPE]

The pipe needs to execute a chain of commands. Inside these commands the can
be multiple redirections from and to files and temporary stuff that get's added
during the reading of a line.

For easier differentiation we want to split up the original token array into
multiple arrays that get used for each line. Each of these arrays can also have
(here document) redirections associated with them.

Inside the pipes there can be syntax execution too 

[CONTROL OPERATORS]

Multiple pipes or commands connected by control operators are referred to as
lists. The control Operators are && and || also known as AND and OR.

	[&&	(AND)]

		cmd1 && cmd2

		The AND control operator makes it so that cmd2 only is executed if
		cmd1 returns an exit status of zero (success).

	[|| (OR)]

		cmd1 || cmd2

		The OR control operator makes it so that cmd2 only is executed if cmd1
		returns a non-zero exit status.

The return value of AND and OR lists is the exit status of the last command
exectued in the list.

[COMPOUND COMMANDS]

A compound commmand is one of the following. In most cases a list in a command's
description may be seperated from the rest of the command by one of more
newlines, and may be followed by a newline in place of a semicolon.

	[ (list) ]

	The list is executed in a subshel. Variable assignments and builtin commands
	that affect the shell's environment do not remain in effect after the
	command completes- The return status is the exit status of list.
